IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb4-common`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part XV, s 190: RIGHT TO DISSENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice Canada consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; not verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS. A shareholder who objects to certain fundamental changes may insist that the
-- corporation buy their shares at "fair value". Subsections (1) and (2) say who may dissent and from what;
-- (3) the entitlement; (4) to (10) the steps the shareholder must take, in order and against the clock;
-- (11) what happens to their rights meanwhile; (12) to (14) the corporation's offer and payment; (15) to
-- (24) the court that fixes the value if they cannot agree; (25) and (26) what happens if the corporation
-- cannot lawfully pay.
--
-- TIME. Every period in this section is a number of calendar days. Each is a `Time limit` of the keel:
-- the day the period runs from counts as day 0, and the last day is that day plus the number of days
-- (keel fork F1). The deadlines are of two kinds, and each has a rule of each kind: "the last day for..."
-- returns a DATE, and "...was sent in time" says whether a given day is within it.
--
-- Section 241 (piece cb5) and the "reasonable grounds" tests of subsection (26) are plain inputs.

§§ `s 190(1) and (2) Who may dissent`

-- src:2358 | Right to dissent
-- src:2359 | 190 (1) Subject to sections 191 and 241, a holder of shares of any class of a corporation may dissent if the corporation is subject to an order under paragraph 192(4)(d) that affects the holder or if the corporation resolves to
-- src:2360 | (a) amend its articles under section 173 or 174 to add, change or remove any provisions restricting or constraining the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of that class;
-- src:2361 | (b) amend its articles under section 173 to add, change or remove any restriction on the business or businesses that the corporation may carry on;
-- src:2362 | (c) amalgamate otherwise than under section 184;
-- src:2363 | (d) be continued under section 188;
-- src:2364 | (e) sell, lease or exchange all or substantially all its property under subsection 189(3); or
-- src:2365 | (f) carry out a going-private transaction or a squeeze-out transaction.
@ref CBCA s 190(1) (src:2359-2365)
DECLARE `Action that gives a right to dissent under s 190(1)` IS ONE OF
    `an order under paragraph 192(4)(d) that affects the holder`
    `a resolution to amend the articles under section 173 or 174 to add, change or remove provisions restricting or constraining the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of that class (s 190(1)(a))`
    `a resolution to amend the articles under section 173 to add, change or remove a restriction on the business or businesses the corporation may carry on (s 190(1)(b))`
    `a resolution to amalgamate otherwise than under section 184 (s 190(1)(c))`
    `a resolution to be continued under section 188 (s 190(1)(d))`
    `a resolution to sell, lease or exchange all or substantially all the property under subsection 189(3) (s 190(1)(e))`
    `a resolution to carry out a going-private transaction or a squeeze-out transaction (s 190(1)(f))`
    `an action that s 190(1) does not list`

-- "Subject to sections 191 and 241": section 191(7) says a shareholder may not dissent from an amendment
-- effected under section 191; section 241 is piece cb5's, so what it displaces is a plain input.
@ref CBCA s 190(1) (src:2359-2365)
GIVEN action IS A `Action that gives a right to dissent under s 190(1)`
      `the provisions concern the holder's class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amendment is effected under section 191` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 241 (piece cb5)
      `section 241 displaces the right to dissent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a holder of shares of a class may dissent within s 190(1)` MEANS
        (CONSIDER action
         WHEN `an order under paragraph 192(4)(d) that affects the holder` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a resolution to amend the articles under section 173 or 174 to add, change or remove provisions restricting or constraining the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of that class (s 190(1)(a))` THEN `the provisions concern the holder's class of shares`
         WHEN `a resolution to amend the articles under section 173 to add, change or remove a restriction on the business or businesses the corporation may carry on (s 190(1)(b))` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a resolution to amalgamate otherwise than under section 184 (s 190(1)(c))` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a resolution to be continued under section 188 (s 190(1)(d))` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a resolution to sell, lease or exchange all or substantially all the property under subsection 189(3) (s 190(1)(e))` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a resolution to carry out a going-private transaction or a squeeze-out transaction (s 190(1)(f))` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND (NOT `the amendment is effected under section 191`)
    AND (NOT `section 241 displaces the right to dissent`)

-- (2): the holder's class or series is entitled to vote under section 176 (the cb4-amendment rule for
-- s 176(1) and s 176(4) answers that), and the corporation resolves to amend its articles in a manner
-- described there.
-- src:2366 | Further right
-- src:2367 | (2) A holder of shares of any class or series of shares entitled to vote under section 176 may dissent if the corporation resolves to amend its articles in a manner described in that section.
@ref CBCA s 190(2) (src:2367)
GIVEN `the holder's class or series is entitled to vote under section 176` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation resolves to amend its articles in a manner described in section 176` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a holder of shares of a class or series may dissent within s 190(2)` MEANS
        `the holder's class or series is entitled to vote under section 176`
    AND `the corporation resolves to amend its articles in a manner described in section 176`

-- (2.1): "even if there is only one class": the answer does not depend on the number of classes.
-- src:2368 | If one class of shares
-- src:2369 | (2.1) The right to dissent described in subsection (2) applies even if there is only one class of shares.
@ref CBCA s 190(2.1) (src:2369)
GIVEN `there is only one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the right in subsection 190(2) applies whatever the number of classes within s 190(2.1)` MEANS TRUE

§§ `s 190(3) and (4) The entitlement`

-- The steps (4), (5), (7), (8) are rules of their own below; subsection (3) asks only whether they were
-- followed. "Subject to subsection (26)" is a separate bar on PAYMENT (see (26)); the entitlement stands.
-- src:2370 | Payment for shares
-- src:2371 | (3) In addition to any other right the shareholder may have, but subject to subsection (26), a shareholder who complies with this section is entitled, when the action approved by the resolution from which the shareholder dissents or an order made under subsection 192(4) becomes effective, to be paid by the corporation the fair value of the shares in respect of which the shareholder dissents, determined as of the close of business on the day before the resolution was adopted or the order was made.
@ref CBCA s 190(3) (src:2371)
GIVEN `the shareholder complies with section 190` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action approved by the resolution, or the order, has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the dissenting shareholder is entitled to be paid the fair value of the shares within s 190(3)` MEANS
        `the shareholder complies with section 190`
    AND `the action approved by the resolution, or the order, has become effective`

-- Fair value is determined as of the close of business on the day before the resolution was adopted or the
-- order was made.
@ref CBCA s 190(3) (src:2371)
GIVEN `the day the resolution was adopted or the order was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day as of which fair value is determined within s 190(3)` MEANS
    `the day immediately before` `the day the resolution was adopted or the order was made`

-- The steps taken, put together: a shareholder "who complies with this section".
@ref CBCA s 190(3), s 190(4), s 190(5), s 190(7), s 190(8) (src:2371 src:2373 src:2375 src:2379 src:2384)
GIVEN `the claim is permitted by subsection 190(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the objection requirement of subsection 190(5) is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand for payment was sent in time and contains what subsection 190(7) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificates were sent in time under subsection 190(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholder has taken every step of s 190` MEANS
        `the claim is permitted by subsection 190(4)`
    AND `the objection requirement of subsection 190(5) is satisfied`
    AND `the demand for payment was sent in time and contains what subsection 190(7) requires`
    AND `the certificates were sent in time under subsection 190(8)`

-- (4): "all the shares of a class held on behalf of any one beneficial owner and registered in the name of
-- the dissenting shareholder": the claim covers exactly those shares, no fewer.
-- src:2372 | No partial dissent
-- src:2373 | (4) A dissenting shareholder may only claim under this section with respect to all the shares of a class held on behalf of any one beneficial owner and registered in the name of the dissenting shareholder.
@ref CBCA s 190(4) (src:2373)
GIVEN `the number of shares of the class that the claim covers` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares of the class held on behalf of that beneficial owner and registered in the shareholder's name` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the claim is permitted within s 190(4)` MEANS
    `the number of shares of the class that the claim covers` EQUALS `the number of shares of the class held on behalf of that beneficial owner and registered in the shareholder's name`

§§ `s 190(5) to (10) The steps the dissenting shareholder takes`

-- (5): the written objection, at or before the meeting, unless the corporation did not give notice of the
-- purpose of the meeting and of the right to dissent.
-- src:2374 | Objection
-- src:2375 | (5) A dissenting shareholder shall send to the corporation, at or before any meeting of shareholders at which a resolution referred to in subsection (1) or (2) is to be voted on, a written objection to the resolution, unless the corporation did not give notice to the shareholder of the purpose of the meeting and of their right to dissent.
@ref CBCA s 190(5) (src:2375)
GIVEN `the shareholder sent the corporation a written objection at or before the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation did not give the shareholder notice of the purpose of the meeting and of the right to dissent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the objection requirement is satisfied within s 190(5)` MEANS
        `the shareholder sent the corporation a written objection at or before the meeting`
    OR  `the corporation did not give the shareholder notice of the purpose of the meeting and of the right to dissent`

-- (6): the corporation's notice that the resolution has been adopted: to each shareholder who filed the
-- objection, but not to one who voted for the resolution or withdrew the objection.
-- src:2376 | Notice of resolution
-- src:2377 | (6) The corporation shall, within ten days after the shareholders adopt the resolution, send to each shareholder who has filed the objection referred to in subsection (5) notice that the resolution has been adopted, but such notice is not required to be sent to any shareholder who voted for the resolution or who has withdrawn their objection.
@ref CBCA s 190(6) (src:2377)
GIVEN `the shareholder filed the objection referred to in subsection 190(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholder voted for the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholder withdrew the objection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must send the shareholder notice that the resolution has been adopted within s 190(6)` MEANS
        `the shareholder filed the objection referred to in subsection 190(5)`
    AND (NOT `the shareholder voted for the resolution`)
    AND (NOT `the shareholder withdrew the objection`)

@ref CBCA s 190(6) (src:2377)
GIVEN `the day the shareholders adopted the resolution` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the corporation to send the notice of adoption within s 190(6)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 10, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day the shareholders adopted the resolution`

@ref CBCA s 190(6) (src:2377)
GIVEN `the day the shareholders adopted the resolution` IS A DATE
      `the day the corporation sent the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice of adoption was sent in time within s 190(6)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 10, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the day the shareholders adopted the resolution` `the day the corporation sent the notice`

-- (7): the demand for payment: twenty days after receiving the (6) notice or, if none was received, twenty
-- days after learning that the resolution had been adopted.
-- src:2378 | Demand for payment
-- src:2379 | (7) A dissenting shareholder shall, within twenty days after receiving a notice under subsection (6) or, if the shareholder does not receive such notice, within twenty days after learning that the resolution has been adopted, send to the corporation a written notice containing
@ref CBCA s 190(7) (src:2379)
GIVEN `the shareholder received a notice under subsection 190(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice under subsection 190(6) was received` IS A DATE
      `the day the shareholder learned that the resolution had been adopted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the twenty days for the demand for payment start within s 190(7)` MEANS
    IF `the shareholder received a notice under subsection 190(6)`
    THEN `the day the notice under subsection 190(6) was received`
    ELSE `the day the shareholder learned that the resolution had been adopted`

@ref CBCA s 190(7) (src:2379)
GIVEN `the day the twenty days start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the shareholder to send the demand for payment within s 190(7)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 20, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day the twenty days start`

@ref CBCA s 190(7) (src:2379)
GIVEN `the day the twenty days start` IS A DATE
      `the day the shareholder sent the demand` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the demand for payment was sent in time within s 190(7)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 20, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the day the twenty days start` `the day the shareholder sent the demand`

-- src:2380 | (a) the shareholder’s name and address;
-- src:2381 | (b) the number and class of shares in respect of which the shareholder dissents; and
-- src:2382 | (c) a demand for payment of the fair value of such shares.
@ref CBCA s 190(7)(a), s 190(7)(b), s 190(7)(c) (src:2380 src:2381 src:2382)
GIVEN `the notice contains the shareholder's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice contains the number and class of shares in respect of which the shareholder dissents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice contains a demand for payment of the fair value of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice contains what s 190(7) requires` MEANS
        `the notice contains the shareholder's name and address`
    AND `the notice contains the number and class of shares in respect of which the shareholder dissents`
    AND `the notice contains a demand for payment of the fair value of those shares`

-- (8): the certificates, within thirty days after sending the (7) notice.
-- src:2383 | Share certificate
-- src:2384 | (8) A dissenting shareholder shall, within thirty days after sending a notice under subsection (7), send the certificates representing the shares in respect of which the shareholder dissents to the corporation or its transfer agent.
@ref CBCA s 190(8) (src:2384)
GIVEN `the day the shareholder sent the notice under subsection 190(7)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the shareholder to send the certificates within s 190(8)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 30, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day the shareholder sent the notice under subsection 190(7)`

@ref CBCA s 190(8) (src:2384)
GIVEN `the day the shareholder sent the notice under subsection 190(7)` IS A DATE
      `the day the shareholder sent the certificates` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the certificates were sent in time within s 190(8)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 30, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the day the shareholder sent the notice under subsection 190(7)` `the day the shareholder sent the certificates`

-- (9): forfeiture.
-- src:2385 | Forfeiture
-- src:2386 | (9) A dissenting shareholder who fails to comply with subsection (8) has no right to make a claim under this section.
@ref CBCA s 190(9) (src:2386)
GIVEN `the shareholder complied with subsection 190(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholder is barred from making a claim within s 190(9)` MEANS
    NOT `the shareholder complied with subsection 190(8)`

-- (10): the corporation or its transfer agent endorses and "forthwith" returns the certificate. "Forthwith"
-- is not turned into a number of days; the duty is encoded as arising on receipt.
-- src:2387 | Endorsing certificate
-- src:2388 | (10) A corporation or its transfer agent shall endorse on any share certificate received under subsection (8) a notice that the holder is a dissenting shareholder under this section and shall forthwith return the share certificates to the dissenting shareholder.
@ref CBCA s 190(10) (src:2388)
GIVEN `the corporation or its transfer agent has received a share certificate under subsection 190(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation or its transfer agent must endorse the certificate and return it within s 190(10)` MEANS
    `the corporation or its transfer agent has received a share certificate under subsection 190(8)`

§§ `s 190(11) Suspension of rights`

-- Rights as a shareholder are suspended from the sending of the (7) notice, except where (a) the
-- shareholder withdraws the notice before the corporation makes an offer, (b) the corporation fails to make
-- an offer in accordance with (12) and the shareholder withdraws the notice, or (c) the directors revoke,
-- terminate or abandon the action. The payment right itself is not a right "as a shareholder".
-- src:2389 | Suspension of rights
-- src:2390 | (11) On sending a notice under subsection (7), a dissenting shareholder ceases to have any rights as a shareholder other than to be paid the fair value of their shares as determined under this section except where
-- src:2391 | (a) the shareholder withdraws that notice before the corporation makes an offer under subsection (12),
-- src:2392 | (b) the corporation fails to make an offer in accordance with subsection (12) and the shareholder withdraws the notice, or
-- src:2393 | (c) the directors revoke a resolution to amend the articles under subsection 173(2) or 174(5), terminate an amalgamation agreement under subsection 183(6) or an application for continuance under subsection 188(6), or abandon a sale, lease or exchange under subsection 189(9),
-- src:2394 | in which case the shareholder’s rights are reinstated as of the date the notice was sent.
@ref CBCA s 190(11) (src:2390-2394)
GIVEN `the shareholder has sent a notice under subsection 190(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholder withdrew the notice before the corporation made an offer under subsection 190(12)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation failed to make an offer in accordance with subsection 190(12)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholder withdrew the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors revoked the resolution, terminated the agreement or application, or abandoned the sale, lease or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholder's rights as a shareholder are reinstated within s 190(11)` MEANS
        `the shareholder has sent a notice under subsection 190(7)`
    AND (    `the shareholder withdrew the notice before the corporation made an offer under subsection 190(12)`
         OR  (    `the corporation failed to make an offer in accordance with subsection 190(12)`
              AND `the shareholder withdrew the notice`)
         OR  `the directors revoked the resolution, terminated the agreement or application, or abandoned the sale, lease or exchange`)

@ref CBCA s 190(11) (src:2390-2394)
GIVEN `the shareholder has sent a notice under subsection 190(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholder withdrew the notice before the corporation made an offer under subsection 190(12)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation failed to make an offer in accordance with subsection 190(12)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholder withdrew the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors revoked the resolution, terminated the agreement or application, or abandoned the sale, lease or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholder has no rights as a shareholder other than to be paid within s 190(11)` MEANS
        `the shareholder has sent a notice under subsection 190(7)`
    AND (NOT (`the shareholder's rights as a shareholder are reinstated within s 190(11)`
                  `the shareholder has sent a notice under subsection 190(7)`
                  `the shareholder withdrew the notice before the corporation made an offer under subsection 190(12)`
                  `the corporation failed to make an offer in accordance with subsection 190(12)`
                  `the shareholder withdrew the notice`
                  `the directors revoked the resolution, terminated the agreement or application, or abandoned the sale, lease or exchange`))

-- "In which case the shareholder's rights are reinstated as of the date the notice was sent": the date
-- from which they count.
@ref CBCA s 190(11) (src:2394)
GIVEN `the day the shareholder sent the notice under subsection 190(7)` IS A DATE
      `the shareholder's rights as a shareholder are reinstated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day from which the reinstated rights count within s 190(11)` MEANS
    IF `the shareholder's rights as a shareholder are reinstated`
    THEN JUST `the day the shareholder sent the notice under subsection 190(7)`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 190(12) to (14) The offer and payment`

-- (12): not later than seven days after the later of the day the action is effective and the day the
-- corporation received the (7) notice.
-- src:2395 | Offer to pay
-- src:2396 | (12) A corporation shall, not later than seven days after the later of the day on which the action approved by the resolution is effective or the day the corporation received the notice referred to in subsection (7), send to each dissenting shareholder who has sent such notice
@ref CBCA s 190(12) (src:2396)
GIVEN `the day the action approved by the resolution became effective` IS A DATE
      `the day the corporation received the notice under subsection 190(7)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the seven days for the offer start within s 190(12)` MEANS
    `the later of two dates` `the day the action approved by the resolution became effective` `the day the corporation received the notice under subsection 190(7)`

@ref CBCA s 190(12) (src:2396)
GIVEN `the day the seven days start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the corporation to send the offer within s 190(12)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 7, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day the seven days start`

@ref CBCA s 190(12) (src:2396)
GIVEN `the day the seven days start` IS A DATE
      `the day the corporation sent the offer or notification` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offer or notification was sent in time within s 190(12)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 7, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the day the seven days start` `the day the corporation sent the offer or notification`

-- (a) a written offer with a statement showing how the fair value was determined; or (b) if (26) applies,
-- a notification that it is unable lawfully to pay.
-- src:2397 | (a) a written offer to pay for their shares in an amount considered by the directors of the corporation to be the fair value, accompanied by a statement showing how the fair value was determined; or
-- src:2398 | (b) if subsection (26) applies, a notification that it is unable lawfully to pay dissenting shareholders for their shares.
@ref CBCA s 190(12)(a), s 190(12)(b) (src:2397 src:2398)
GIVEN `the corporation sent a written offer to pay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer is for an amount the directors consider to be the fair value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer is accompanied by a statement showing how the fair value was determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 190(26) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation sent a notification that it is unable lawfully to pay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation's response to the dissenting shareholder complies with s 190(12)` MEANS
        (    `the corporation sent a written offer to pay`
         AND `the offer is for an amount the directors consider to be the fair value`
         AND `the offer is accompanied by a statement showing how the fair value was determined`)
    OR  (    `subsection 190(26) applies`
         AND `the corporation sent a notification that it is unable lawfully to pay`)

-- (13).
-- src:2399 | Same terms
-- src:2400 | (13) Every offer made under subsection (12) for shares of the same class or series shall be on the same terms.
@ref CBCA s 190(13) (src:2400)
GIVEN `the offers are for shares of the same class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offers are on the same terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offers comply with s 190(13)` MEANS
        (NOT `the offers are for shares of the same class or series`)
    OR  `the offers are on the same terms`

-- (14): payment within ten days after the offer is accepted, subject to (26); the offer lapses if no
-- acceptance is received within thirty days after it is made.
-- src:2401 | Payment
-- src:2402 | (14) Subject to subsection (26), a corporation shall pay for the shares of a dissenting shareholder within ten days after an offer made under subsection (12) has been accepted, but any such offer lapses if the corporation does not receive an acceptance thereof within thirty days after the offer has been made.
@ref CBCA s 190(14) (src:2402)
GIVEN `the offer has been accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 190(26) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must pay for the shares within s 190(14)` MEANS
        `the offer has been accepted`
    AND (NOT `subsection 190(26) applies`)

@ref CBCA s 190(14) (src:2402)
GIVEN `the day the offer was accepted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the corporation to pay within s 190(14)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 10, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day the offer was accepted`

@ref CBCA s 190(14) (src:2402)
GIVEN `the day the offer was accepted` IS A DATE
      `the day the corporation paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the payment was made in time within s 190(14)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 10, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the day the offer was accepted` `the day the corporation paid`

@ref CBCA s 190(14) (src:2402)
GIVEN `the day the offer was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the corporation to receive an acceptance within s 190(14)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 30, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day the offer was made`

-- Lapse: an acceptance received in time keeps the offer alive; otherwise it lapses once the thirty days
-- have run out (a late acceptance does not revive it).
@ref CBCA s 190(14) (src:2402)
GIVEN `the day the offer was made` IS A DATE
      `an acceptance has been received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the acceptance was received` IS A DATE
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the offer has lapsed on a day within s 190(14)` MEANS
        (NOT (    `an acceptance has been received`
              AND `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 30, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the day the offer was made` `the day the acceptance was received`))
    AND `the day I am asking about` GREATER THAN (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 30, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day the offer was made`)

§§ `s 190(15) to (24) The court`

-- (15): the corporation may apply to a court within fifty days after the action is effective, or within a
-- further period the court allows, if it failed to make an offer or the shareholder failed to accept.
-- src:2403 | Corporation may apply to court
-- src:2404 | (15) Where a corporation fails to make an offer under subsection (12), or if a dissenting shareholder fails to accept an offer, the corporation may, within fifty days after the action approved by the resolution is effective or within such further period as a court may allow, apply to a court to fix a fair value for the shares of any dissenting shareholder.
@ref CBCA s 190(15) (src:2404)
GIVEN `the corporation failed to make an offer under subsection 190(12)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dissenting shareholder failed to accept an offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the action approved by the resolution became effective` IS A DATE
      `the day the corporation applied to the court` IS A DATE
      `a court has allowed a further period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the further period the court allowed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may apply to a court to fix a fair value within s 190(15)` MEANS
        (    `the corporation failed to make an offer under subsection 190(12)`
         OR  `the dissenting shareholder failed to accept an offer`)
    AND (    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 50, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the day the action approved by the resolution became effective` `the day the corporation applied to the court`
         OR  (    `a court has allowed a further period`
              AND `the day the corporation applied to the court` AT LEAST `the day the action approved by the resolution became effective`
              AND `the day the corporation applied to the court` AT MOST `the last day of the further period the court allowed`))

@ref CBCA s 190(15) (src:2404)
GIVEN `the day the action approved by the resolution became effective` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the corporation to apply to a court within s 190(15)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 50, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day the action approved by the resolution became effective`

-- (16): if the corporation does not apply, the shareholder may apply within a FURTHER twenty days (fork F4:
-- the twenty days follow the end of the corporation's fifty), or within such further period as a court
-- allows. The shareholder cannot apply before the corporation has "failed", that is, before the fifty
-- days are over.
-- src:2405 | Shareholder application to court
-- src:2406 | (16) If a corporation fails to apply to a court under subsection (15), a dissenting shareholder may apply to a court for the same purpose within a further period of twenty days or within such further period as a court may allow.
@ref CBCA s 190(16) (src:2406)
GIVEN `the corporation failed to apply to a court under subsection 190(15)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the action approved by the resolution became effective` IS A DATE
      `the day the dissenting shareholder applied to the court` IS A DATE
      `a court has allowed a further period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the further period the court allowed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the dissenting shareholder may apply to a court to fix a fair value within s 190(16)` MEANS
        `the corporation failed to apply to a court under subsection 190(15)`
    AND `the day the dissenting shareholder applied to the court` GREATER THAN (`the last day for the corporation to apply to a court within s 190(15)` `the day the action approved by the resolution became effective`)
    AND (    `the day the dissenting shareholder applied to the court` AT MOST (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 20, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` (`the last day for the corporation to apply to a court within s 190(15)` `the day the action approved by the resolution became effective`))
         OR  (    `a court has allowed a further period`
              AND `the day the dissenting shareholder applied to the court` AT MOST `the last day of the further period the court allowed`))

@ref CBCA s 190(16) (src:2406)
GIVEN `the day the action approved by the resolution became effective` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the dissenting shareholder to apply to a court within s 190(16)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 20, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` (`the last day for the corporation to apply to a court within s 190(15)` `the day the action approved by the resolution became effective`)

-- (17): the venue.
-- src:2407 | Venue
-- src:2408 | (17) An application under subsection (15) or (16) shall be made to a court having jurisdiction in the place where the corporation has its registered office or in the province where the dissenting shareholder resides if the corporation carries on business in that province.
@ref CBCA s 190(17) (src:2408)
GIVEN `the court has jurisdiction in the place where the corporation has its registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has jurisdiction in the province where the dissenting shareholder resides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation carries on business in that province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court is a proper court within s 190(17)` MEANS
        `the court has jurisdiction in the place where the corporation has its registered office`
    OR  (    `the court has jurisdiction in the province where the dissenting shareholder resides`
         AND `the corporation carries on business in that province`)

-- (18): for an application under (15) or (16), no security for costs; for any other application the
-- subsection says nothing.
-- src:2409 | No security for costs
-- src:2410 | (18) A dissenting shareholder is not required to give security for costs in an application made under subsection (15) or (16).
@ref CBCA s 190(18) (src:2410)
GIVEN `the application is made under subsection 190(15) or 190(16)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a dissenting shareholder is required to give security for costs within s 190(18)` MEANS
    IF `the application is made under subsection 190(15) or 190(16)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- (19).
-- src:2411 | Parties
-- src:2412 | (19) On an application to a court under subsection (15) or (16),
-- src:2413 | (a) all dissenting shareholders whose shares have not been purchased by the corporation shall be joined as parties and are bound by the decision of the court; and
-- src:2414 | (b) the corporation shall notify each affected dissenting shareholder of the date, place and consequences of the application and of their right to appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 190(19)(a) (src:2413)
GIVEN `the dissenting shareholder's shares have not been purchased by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the dissenting shareholder must be joined as a party and is bound by the decision within s 190(19)(a)` MEANS
    `the dissenting shareholder's shares have not been purchased by the corporation`

@ref CBCA s 190(19)(b) (src:2414)
GIVEN `the notice states the date of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the place of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the consequences of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the shareholder's right to appear and be heard in person or by counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation's notice to the dissenting shareholder complies with s 190(19)(b)` MEANS
        `the notice states the date of the application`
    AND `the notice states the place of the application`
    AND `the notice states the consequences of the application`
    AND `the notice states the shareholder's right to appear and be heard in person or by counsel`

-- (20) to (23): the court's powers and the final order. The court's powers are encoded for what they mean
-- to the shareholder: the value is fixed for ALL dissenting shareholders; the order runs against the
-- corporation; interest is in the court's discretion between the day the action is effective and the day
-- of payment.
-- src:2415 | Powers of court
-- src:2416 | (20) On an application to a court under subsection (15) or (16), the court may determine whether any other person is a dissenting shareholder who should be joined as a party, and the court shall then fix a fair value for the shares of all dissenting shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 190(20) (src:2416)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 190(15) or 190(16)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court must fix a fair value for the shares of all dissenting shareholders within s 190(20)` MEANS
    `an application has been made under subsection 190(15) or 190(16)`

-- src:2417 | Appraisers
-- src:2418 | (21) A court may in its discretion appoint one or more appraisers to assist the court to fix a fair value for the shares of the dissenting shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 190(21) (src:2418)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 190(15) or 190(16)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may appoint appraisers within s 190(21)` MEANS
    `an application has been made under subsection 190(15) or 190(16)`

-- src:2419 | Final order
-- src:2420 | (22) The final order of a court shall be rendered against the corporation in favour of each dissenting shareholder and for the amount of the shares as fixed by the court.
@ref CBCA s 190(22) (src:2420)
GIVEN `the court has fixed a fair value for the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the final order is rendered against the corporation in favour of each dissenting shareholder within s 190(22)` MEANS
    `the court has fixed a fair value for the shares`

-- src:2421 | Interest
-- src:2422 | (23) A court may in its discretion allow a reasonable rate of interest on the amount payable to each dissenting shareholder from the date the action approved by the resolution is effective until the date of payment.
@ref CBCA s 190(23) (src:2422)
GIVEN `the day the action approved by the resolution became effective` IS A DATE
      `the day of payment` IS A DATE
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may allow interest for a day within s 190(23)` MEANS
        `the day I am asking about` AT LEAST `the day the action approved by the resolution became effective`
    AND `the day I am asking about` AT MOST `the day of payment`

-- (24): if (26) applies, within ten days after the pronouncement of the (22) order the corporation notifies
-- each dissenting shareholder that it is unable lawfully to pay.
-- src:2423 | Notice that subsection (26) applies
-- src:2424 | (24) If subsection (26) applies, the corporation shall, within ten days after the pronouncement of an order under subsection (22), notify each dissenting shareholder that it is unable lawfully to pay dissenting shareholders for their shares.
@ref CBCA s 190(24) (src:2424)
GIVEN `subsection 190(26) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court has pronounced an order under subsection 190(22)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must notify each dissenting shareholder that it is unable lawfully to pay within s 190(24)` MEANS
        `subsection 190(26) applies`
    AND `a court has pronounced an order under subsection 190(22)`

@ref CBCA s 190(24) (src:2424)
GIVEN `the day the court pronounced the order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the corporation to give the notice within s 190(24)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 10, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day the court pronounced the order`

@ref CBCA s 190(24) (src:2424)
GIVEN `the day the court pronounced the order` IS A DATE
      `the day the corporation gave the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice was given in time within s 190(24)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 10, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the day the court pronounced the order` `the day the corporation gave the notice`

§§ `s 190(25) and (26) Where the corporation cannot lawfully pay`

-- (25): the choice. The Act does not say what follows if the shareholder does not deliver a written notice
-- in time, or if (26) does not apply, so those cases are a named answer.
-- src:2425 | Effect where subsection (26) applies
-- src:2426 | (25) If subsection (26) applies, a dissenting shareholder, by written notice delivered to the corporation within thirty days after receiving a notice under subsection (24), may
-- src:2427 | (a) withdraw their notice of dissent, in which case the corporation is deemed to consent to the withdrawal and the shareholder is reinstated to their full rights as a shareholder; or
-- src:2428 | (b) retain a status as a claimant against the corporation, to be paid as soon as the corporation is lawfully able to do so or, in a liquidation, to be ranked subordinate to the rights of creditors of the corporation but in priority to its shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 190(25) (src:2426-2428)
DECLARE `Choice of a dissenting shareholder under s 190(25)` IS ONE OF
    `to withdraw the notice of dissent`
    `to retain a status as a claimant against the corporation`

DECLARE `Effect of the choice of a dissenting shareholder under s 190(25)` IS ONE OF
    `the corporation is deemed to consent to the withdrawal and the shareholder is reinstated to their full rights as a shareholder`
    `the shareholder is a claimant, paid as soon as the corporation is lawfully able to do so, or in a liquidation ranked after the creditors and before the shareholders`
    `the Act does not say what the effect is`

@ref CBCA s 190(25) (src:2426-2428)
GIVEN `the day the shareholder received the notice under subsection 190(24)` IS A DATE
      `the day the shareholder delivered the written notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the written notice was delivered in time within s 190(25)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 30, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `the day the shareholder received the notice under subsection 190(24)` `the day the shareholder delivered the written notice`

@ref CBCA s 190(25) (src:2426-2428)
GIVEN `the day the shareholder received the notice under subsection 190(24)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the shareholder to deliver the written notice within s 190(25)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 30, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day the shareholder received the notice under subsection 190(24)`

@ref CBCA s 190(25) (src:2426-2428)
GIVEN `subsection 190(26) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the written notice was delivered in time` IS A BOOLEAN
      choice IS A `Choice of a dissenting shareholder under s 190(25)`
GIVETH A `Effect of the choice of a dissenting shareholder under s 190(25)`
`the effect of the shareholder's choice within s 190(25)` MEANS
    IF `subsection 190(26) applies` AND `the written notice was delivered in time`
    THEN (CONSIDER choice
          WHEN `to withdraw the notice of dissent` THEN `the corporation is deemed to consent to the withdrawal and the shareholder is reinstated to their full rights as a shareholder`
          WHEN `to retain a status as a claimant against the corporation` THEN `the shareholder is a claimant, paid as soon as the corporation is lawfully able to do so, or in a liquidation ranked after the creditors and before the shareholders`)
    ELSE `the Act does not say what the effect is`

-- (26): the bar on payment. Note that limb (b) compares the realizable value of the assets with the
-- liabilities alone; the stated capital of all classes, which the insolvency test of s 192(2)(b) adds, is
-- not part of this test.
-- src:2429 | Limitation
-- src:2430 | (26) A corporation shall not make a payment to a dissenting shareholder under this section if there are reasonable grounds for believing that
-- src:2431 | (a) the corporation is or would after the payment be unable to pay its liabilities as they become due; or
-- src:2432 | (b) the realizable value of the corporation’s assets would thereby be less than the aggregate of its liabilities.
@ref CBCA s 190(26) (src:2430-2432)
GIVEN `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation is or would after the payment be unable to pay its liabilities as they become due` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the realizable value of the corporation's assets would thereby be less than the aggregate of its liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must not make a payment to a dissenting shareholder within s 190(26)` MEANS
        `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation is or would after the payment be unable to pay its liabilities as they become due`
    OR  `there are reasonable grounds for believing that the realizable value of the corporation's assets would thereby be less than the aggregate of its liabilities`
